                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "TL;DR Point and click strategy - continued\r\n\r\nWot I liked\r\n- There's a story;\r\n- Most of the positive things told about the main game apply here: some exploration, some plot, fun micro;\r\n- Day and night cycle;\r\n- A bunch of quests that improve on the old formula;\r\n- Some puzzles;\r\n- Cool looking dragons.\r\n\r\nWot I disliked\r\n- Microcontrol - you misclick all the times due to poor frames;\r\n- Base game graphics looks decent for 00s, but addons were released in 10s and the facelift they had done was bad;\r\n- Big combats are totally uncontrollable;\r\n- The game misses the strategy features that most decent strategies had in 1990s;\r\n- Itemization is poor. Your team grows in size to 6-7 people all wearing odds and ends. Moreover there're no merchants so most of my team had to spec for items not the other way around;\r\n- The story ends on a cliffhanger;\r\n- The game has no business being a standalone title - it's a 3-4 map experince;\r\n- AI is still primitive;\r\n- The best strategy still is to amass ranged / flying units.\r\n\r\nTo sum it all up, more of the same, a lot of flaws, but I liked it.",
